Sval: accessibility takes a hanging document off its parent's child list

`OuterDocAccessible::Shutdown` detaches its child document and queues it to
be bound to the parent again (`BindChildDocument`), but leaves it in the
parent's `mChildDocuments`. The rebind in
`NotificationController::WillRefresh` appends it a second time on success;
on failure it shuts the child down, and `DocAccessible::Shutdown` removes
only a child that has a parent, so the dead child stays listed. A
window-modal dialog's frame goes this way when the dialog closes with
accessibility on: after eight dialogs had opened and closed, a window's
document listed three dead documents. When accessibility starts while such a
dialog is up, the window's document is not yet loaded, and a listed child
that never loads keeps it from loading: it stays busy, and its notification
controller observes every refresh, holding vsync on until accessibility
shuts down. Reading the state of the dead child that
`nsIAccessibleDocument.getChildDocumentAt` returns crashes the process.
Taking every hanging document off the list before it is bound or shut down
keeps the list to the children in the tree.

diff --git a/accessible/base/NotificationController.cpp b/accessible/base/NotificationController.cpp
index 40a49c0605..96289c808d 100644
--- a/accessible/base/NotificationController.cpp
+++ b/accessible/base/NotificationController.cpp
@@ -917,6 +917,14 @@ void NotificationController::WillRefresh(mozilla::TimeStamp aTime) {
   nsTArray<RefPtr<DocAccessible>> newChildDocs;
   for (uint32_t idx = 0; idx < hangingDocCnt; idx++) {
     DocAccessible* childDoc = mHangingChildDocuments[idx];
+    // A hanging document is out of this document's tree, so it is out of the
+    // list of child documents too. OuterDocAccessible::Shutdown queues its
+    // child here while the child is still listed, and DocAccessible::Shutdown
+    // takes only a bound child off the list. Left listed, the child is listed
+    // twice once bound again, or stays listed after its shutdown, and while a
+    // listed child is not completely loaded this document's load is never
+    // processed: it stays busy and observes every refresh.
+    mDocument->RemoveChildDocument(childDoc);
     if (childDoc->IsDefunct()) {
       continue;
     }
